  <!-- Appearance -->
  <s:String x:Key="TabAppearance">Manage Themes</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="ThemeListLabel">Themes</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="LiveThemeMarker">IN USE</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="ApplyTheme">Apply</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="ThemePreviewHelp">Selecting a theme previews it on this window. Click Apply to keep it - leaving this tab puts back the one in use.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="PresetThemeNote">This theme came with the application and cannot be edited. Clone it to make a version you can change.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="DeleteThemeQuestion">Delete the theme "{0}"?</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="DeleteAppliedTheme">"{0}" is the theme in use. Deleting it switches back to Dark. Delete it?</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotShell">Shell</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotPane">Pane</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotAccent">Accent</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotHighlight">Highlight</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotShellHelp">The window's background color, used exactly as picked. The panes, borders and text follow from it, keeping the same contrast whatever color you choose. Drag the saturation to nothing for plain gray.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotPaneHelp">The panels that sit on the window - the two assignment lists, the device, the libraries. How far it stands off the shell is the difference between one flat surface and cards laid on a desk. Row borders and hover fills follow it.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotAccentHelp">Frames every pane, draws the device and marks the keymap in use. Avoid green and red: those stay reserved for whether the pad is running.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotHighlightHelp">Marks the control you are editing, and its row in the list. Pick something unmistakable against the accent.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotLive">Live</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotLiveHelp">Flashes on a control, and on its row, while you are holding that key down on the pad. Separate from the highlight so that pressing the control you are already editing still shows something.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="ThemeIsInUse">In use. Color changes take effect straight away and are saved as you make them.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="ThemePreviewing">Previewing. Color changes are saved to this theme, but the application goes back to the theme in use when you leave this page - click Apply to keep this one.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotShellTip">The window itself: the background behind every page, the status bar along the bottom, and the inside of text boxes, dropdowns and lists. The text colors are worked out from it, so a light shell gives dark text on its own.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotPaneTip">The panels sitting on the window: both assignment lists and the device on Assign Buttons, the profile and macro libraries, the toolbar, and the menu a dropdown opens. Row borders and the shading under whatever you are pointing at are worked out from it.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotAccentTip">Structure and emphasis: the border around every panel, the drawing of the device itself, the page tab you are on, the keymap in use, the check mark in a checkbox, and the settings-file link in the status bar.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotHighlightTip">Whatever is being edited: the selected row in the assignment lists, its outline on the device drawing, the selected entry in any library - profiles, macros, steps, themes - and the border of a text box you are typing in.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotLiveTip">Appears only while a key is physically held down on the pad: the control on the drawing and its row in the list both flash this, then go back. Keep it clear of the highlight, or pressing the key you are already editing will be hard to see.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="ThemeListTip">The themes that came with the application, then the ones you have made. Click one to see it on the real window - nothing is kept until you press Apply.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="NewThemeTip">Starts a new theme, taking its colors from the one being previewed - so you begin from something close rather than from nothing.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="ApplyThemeTip">Keeps the theme you are previewing. Until you press this, the window goes back to the theme in use as soon as you leave this page. Color changes are saved either way.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="PickerFieldTip">Drag to set how strong the color is, left to right, and how bright, top to bottom. The window recolors as you drag, so you can judge a color where it will actually be used.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="PickerSpectrumTip">Drag to choose the hue the square above works from.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="PickerHexTip">The color written the usual way, as #RRGGBB. Type or paste one to set it exactly.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="PickerChannelTip">Red, green and blue, each from 0 to 255. Type a value to set the color exactly.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="PickerPreviewTip">The color currently chosen for the element selected above.</s:String>

