  <s:String x:Key="SlotText">Text</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotTextTip">The color of the words on screen. Leave it alone and it is worked out from Shell - near-white on a dark theme, near-black on a light one - which is what keeps any theme readable. Set it and that guarantee is yours to keep.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="SlotTextHelp">Body text. Dim text follows it automatically, the same distance toward the shell that the derived pair has always used, so help text and the small markers stay in step with whatever you pick. Only Shell and Pane decide readability, so check this one against both.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="TextGroupLabel">Text size (applies to the whole program)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="ColorGroupLabel">Colors</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="FontSizeLabel">Size</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="FontSizeTip">Text size for the whole application, not for the theme you have selected. Headings, help text and the small markers sit at fixed distances from it, so they all move together. Limited to 10-16: parts of the window are laid out to fixed widths, and text larger than that would be clipped rather than wrapped.&#x0a;&#x0a;The typeface itself is not a choice - it is whatever Windows uses for its own message text.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="MenuUseAsFallback">Use when no program matches</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="FallbackMarker">FALLBACK</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="FallbackProfileTip">The profile the pad falls back to when auto-switch finds no program that claims one. Right-click any profile to move it here.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="LockedProfileNote">This profile leaves every control at its controller default, in all eight keymaps, and cannot be changed. It is here so there is always a way back to a plain pad. Clone it to start a layout of your own.</s:String>
